# BS1 (run 1 of 3): the AUDITS-OFF HANG SHAPES at four users on c2-packed-tp4-best-ship, the traffic candidate (the nine levers, the in-trace sampler, production limits, no gate marker).
# The shapes: concurrent4_steady, steady_resend (an engine build after many packed rounds), replay_concurrent4 (a rows=2 sequential replay) and the exactness reference concurrent4_code_equal.
# Each run follows its own all-four reset. READ: three CONSECUTIVE completions (BS1 to BS3), every user at budget, c2_smoke_check clean, no watchdog or replay-deadline exit, the
# concurrent4_code_equal content and reasoning hashes equal in every run and equal to the previous window's best-ship hashes. No stall watch on this profile: a stall waits for the job
# timeout and records nothing, which is itself the finding. Duration (estimate): 45 min. Stop rule: one stall stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-5 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-5 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-5 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-ship
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,concurrent4_code_equal
